{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-table"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing\nstate the \"angular signals\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-table"},{"type":"text","value":" re-exports all of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/table-core"},{"type":"text","value":"'s APIs and the following:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createangulartable","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAngularTable"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepts an options function or a computed value that returns the table options, and returns a table."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {createAngularTable} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nexport class AppComponent {\n  data = signal<Person[]>([])\n\n  table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n    data: this.data(),\n    columns: defaultColumns,\n    getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  }))\n}\n\n// ...render your table in template\n","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An Angular structural directive for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FlexRender supports any type of content supported by Angular:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A string, or a html string via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"innerHTML"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"https://angular.dev/api/core/TemplateRef","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TemplateRef"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"https://angular.dev/api/core/Component","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component"}]},{"type":"text","value":" wrapped into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRenderComponent"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can just use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.renderValue"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getValue"},{"type":"text","value":" APIs to render the cells of your table. However,\nthese APIs will only spit out the raw cell values (from accessor functions).\nIf you are using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell: () => any"},{"type":"text","value":" column definition options, you will want to use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRenderDirective"},{"type":"text","value":" from the adapter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell column definition is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"reactive"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and runs into an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"injection context"}]},{"type":"text","value":", then you can inject services or make use of signals to automatically modify the rendered content."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({\n  imports: [FlexRenderDirective],\n  //...\n})\nclass YourComponent {}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"\n<tbody>\n@for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n  <tr>\n    @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container\n          *flexRender=\"\n              cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n              props: cell.getContext();\n              let cell\n            \"\n        >\n          <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n          {{ cell }}\n          <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n          <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n    }\n  </tr>\n}\n</tbody>","lang":"angular-html"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"rendering-a-component","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering a Component"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To render a Component into a specific column header/cell/footer, you can pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRenderComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" instantiated with\nyour `ComponentType, with the ability to include parameters such as inputs, outputs and a custom injector."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {flexRenderComponent} from \"./flex-render-component\";\nimport {ChangeDetectionStrategy, input, output} from \"@angular/core\";\n\n@Component({\n  template: `\n    ...\n  `,\n  standalone: true,\n  changeDetectionStrategy: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n  host: {\n    '(click)': 'clickEvent.emit($event)'\n  }\n})\nclass CustomCell {\n  readonly content = input.required<string>();\n  readonly cellType = input<MyType>();\n\n  // An output that will emit for every cell click\n  readonly clickEvent = output<Event>();\n}\n\nclass AppComponent {\n  columns: ColumnDef<unknown>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'custom-cell',\n      header: () => {\n        const translateService = inject(TranslateService);\n        return translateService.translate('...');\n      },\n      cell: (context) => {\n        return flexRenderComponent(\n          MyCustomComponent,\n          {\n            injector, // Optional injector\n            inputs: {\n              // Mandatory input since we are using `input.required()\n              content: context.row.original.rowProperty,\n              // cellType? - Optional input\n            },\n            outputs: {\n              clickEvent: () => {\n                // Do something\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        )\n      },\n    },\n  ]\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Underneath, this utilizes\nthe "},{"type":"link","href":"https://angular.dev/api/core/ViewContainerRef#createComponent","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ViewContainerRef#createComponent"}]},{"type":"text","value":" api.\nTherefore, you should declare your custom inputs using the @Input decorator or input/model signals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can still access the table cell context through the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectFlexRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":" function, which returns the context\nvalue based on the props you pass to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRenderDirective"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"\n@Component({\n  // ...\n})\nclass CustomCellComponent {\n  // context of a cell component\n  readonly context = injectFlexRenderContext<CellContext<TData, TValue>>();\n  // context of a header/footer component\n  readonly context = injectFlexRenderContext<HeaderContext<TData, TValue>>();\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, you can render a component into a specific column header, cell, or footer by passing the component type\nto the corresponding column definitions. These column definitions will be provided to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" directive along\nwith the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"class AppComponent {\n  columns: ColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'select',\n      header: () => TableHeadSelectionComponent<Person>,\n      cell: () => TableRowSelectionComponent<Person>,\n    },\n  ]\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<ng-container\n  *flexRender=\"\n    header.column.columnDef.header;\n    props: header.getContext();\n    let headerCell\n  \"\n>\n  {{ headerCell }}\n</ng-container>","lang":"angular-html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" provided in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" directive will be accessible to your component.\nYou can explicitly define the context properties required by your component.\nIn this example, the context provided to flexRender is of type HeaderContext.\nInput signal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table"},{"type":"text","value":", which is a property of HeaderContext together with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":" properties,\nis then defined to be used in the component. If any of the context properties are\nneeded in your component, feel free to use them. Please take note that only input signal is supported,\nwhen defining access to context properties, using this approach."}]},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({\n  template: `\n    <input\n      type=\"checkbox\"\n      [checked]=\"table().getIsAllRowsSelected()\"\n      [indeterminate]=\"table().getIsSomeRowsSelected()\"\n      (change)=\"table().toggleAllRowsSelected()\"\n    />\n  `,\n  // ...\n})\nexport class TableHeadSelectionComponent<T> {\n  //column = input.required<Column<T, unknown>>()\n  //header = input.required<Header<T, unknown>>()\n  table = input.required<Table<T>>()\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"rendering-a-templateref","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering a TemplateRef"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In order to render a TemplateRef into a specific column header/cell/footer, you can pass the TemplateRef into the column\ndefinition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can access the TemplateRef data via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$implicit"},{"type":"text","value":" property, which is valued based on what is passed in the props\nfield of flexRender."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In most cases, each TemplateRef will be rendered with the $implicit context valued based on the cell type in this way:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Header: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HeaderContext<T, ?>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CellContext<T, ?>"},{"type":"text","value":","}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Footer: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HeaderContext<T, ?>"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"\n<ng-container\n  *flexRender=\"\n              cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n              props: cell.getContext();\n              let cell\n            \"\n>\n  <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n  {{ cell }}\n  <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n  <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n</ng-container>\n\n<ng-template #myCell let-context>\n  <!-- render something with context -->\n</ng-template>","lang":"angular-html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type {\n  CellContext,\n  ColumnDef,\n  HeaderContext,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport {Component, TemplateRef, viewChild} from '@angular/core'\n\n@Component({\n  template: `\n    <tbody>\n      @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n        <tr>\n          @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n            <td>\n              <ng-container\n                *flexRender=\"\n                  cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n                  props: cell.getContext(); // Data given to the TemplateRef\n                  let cell\n                \"\n              >\n                <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n                {{ cell }}\n                <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n                <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n              </ng-container>\n            </td>\n          }\n        </tr>\n      }\n    </tbody>\n\n    <ng-template #customHeader let-context>\n      {{ context.getValue() }}\n    </ng-template>\n    <ng-template #customCell let-context>\n      {{ context.getValue() }}\n    </ng-template>\n  `,\n})\nclass AppComponent {\n  customHeader =\n    viewChild.required<TemplateRef<{ $implicit: HeaderContext<any, any> }>>(\n      'customHeader'\n    )\n  customCell =\n    viewChild.required<TemplateRef<{ $implicit: CellContext<any, any> }>>(\n      'customCell'\n    )\n\n  columns: ColumnDef<unknown>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'customCell',\n      header: () => this.customHeader(),\n      cell: () => this.customCell(),\n    },\n  ]\n}","lang":"angular-ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"exports","text":"Exports","level":2},{"id":"createangulartable","text":"createAngularTable","level":3},{"id":"flexrender","text":"FlexRender","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"rendering-a-component","text":"Rendering a Component","level":4},{"id":"rendering-a-templateref","text":"Rendering a TemplateRef","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `@tanstack/angular-table` adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing\nstate the \"angular signals\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates.\n\n## Exports\n\n`@tanstack/angular-table` re-exports all of `@tanstack/table-core`'s APIs and the following:\n\n### `createAngularTable`\n\nAccepts an options function or a computed value that returns the table options, and returns a table.\n\n```ts\nimport {createAngularTable} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nexport class AppComponent {\n  data = signal<Person[]>([])\n\n  table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n    data: this.data(),\n    columns: defaultColumns,\n    getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  }))\n}\n\n// ...render your table in template\n\n```\n\n### `FlexRender`\n\nAn Angular structural directive for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values.\n\nFlexRender supports any type of content supported by Angular:\n\n- A string, or a html string via `innerHTML`\n- A [TemplateRef](https://angular.dev/api/core/TemplateRef)\n- A [Component](https://angular.dev/api/core/Component) wrapped into `FlexRenderComponent`\n\nYou can just use the `cell.renderValue` or `cell.getValue` APIs to render the cells of your table. However,\nthese APIs will only spit out the raw cell values (from accessor functions).\nIf you are using the `cell: () => any` column definition options, you will want to use the `FlexRenderDirective` from the adapter.\n\nCell column definition is **reactive** and runs into an **injection context**, then you can inject services or make use of signals to automatically modify the rendered content.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\n@Component({\n  imports: [FlexRenderDirective],\n  //...\n})\nclass YourComponent {}\n```\n\n```angular-html\n\n<tbody>\n@for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n  <tr>\n    @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container\n          *flexRender=\"\n              cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n              props: cell.getContext();\n              let cell\n            \"\n        >\n          <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n          {{ cell }}\n          <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n          <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n    }\n  </tr>\n}\n</tbody>\n```\n\n#### Rendering a Component\n\nTo render a Component into a specific column header/cell/footer, you can pass a `FlexRenderComponent` instantiated with\nyour `ComponentType, with the ability to include parameters such as inputs, outputs and a custom injector.\n\n```ts\nimport {flexRenderComponent} from \"./flex-render-component\";\nimport {ChangeDetectionStrategy, input, output} from \"@angular/core\";\n\n@Component({\n  template: `\n    ...\n  `,\n  standalone: true,\n  changeDetectionStrategy: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n  host: {\n    '(click)': 'clickEvent.emit($event)'\n  }\n})\nclass CustomCell {\n  readonly content = input.required<string>();\n  readonly cellType = input<MyType>();\n\n  // An output that will emit for every cell click\n  readonly clickEvent = output<Event>();\n}\n\nclass AppComponent {\n  columns: ColumnDef<unknown>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'custom-cell',\n      header: () => {\n        const translateService = inject(TranslateService);\n        return translateService.translate('...');\n      },\n      cell: (context) => {\n        return flexRenderComponent(\n          MyCustomComponent,\n          {\n            injector, // Optional injector\n            inputs: {\n              // Mandatory input since we are using `input.required()\n              content: context.row.original.rowProperty,\n              // cellType? - Optional input\n            },\n            outputs: {\n              clickEvent: () => {\n                // Do something\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        )\n      },\n    },\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nUnderneath, this utilizes\nthe [ViewContainerRef#createComponent](https://angular.dev/api/core/ViewContainerRef#createComponent) api.\nTherefore, you should declare your custom inputs using the @Input decorator or input/model signals.\n\nYou can still access the table cell context through the `injectFlexRenderContext` function, which returns the context\nvalue based on the props you pass to the `FlexRenderDirective`.\n\n```ts\n\n@Component({\n  // ...\n})\nclass CustomCellComponent {\n  // context of a cell component\n  readonly context = injectFlexRenderContext<CellContext<TData, TValue>>();\n  // context of a header/footer component\n  readonly context = injectFlexRenderContext<HeaderContext<TData, TValue>>();\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, you can render a component into a specific column header, cell, or footer by passing the component type\nto the corresponding column definitions. These column definitions will be provided to the `flexRender` directive along\nwith the `context`.\n\n```ts\nclass AppComponent {\n  columns: ColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'select',\n      header: () => TableHeadSelectionComponent<Person>,\n      cell: () => TableRowSelectionComponent<Person>,\n    },\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n```angular-html\n<ng-container\n  *flexRender=\"\n    header.column.columnDef.header;\n    props: header.getContext();\n    let headerCell\n  \"\n>\n  {{ headerCell }}\n</ng-container>\n```\n\nProperties of `context` provided in the `flexRender` directive will be accessible to your component.\nYou can explicitly define the context properties required by your component.\nIn this example, the context provided to flexRender is of type HeaderContext.\nInput signal `table`, which is a property of HeaderContext together with `column` and `header` properties,\nis then defined to be used in the component. If any of the context properties are\nneeded in your component, feel free to use them. Please take note that only input signal is supported,\nwhen defining access to context properties, using this approach.\n\n```angular-ts\n@Component({\n  template: `\n    <input\n      type=\"checkbox\"\n      [checked]=\"table().getIsAllRowsSelected()\"\n      [indeterminate]=\"table().getIsSomeRowsSelected()\"\n      (change)=\"table().toggleAllRowsSelected()\"\n    />\n  `,\n  // ...\n})\nexport class TableHeadSelectionComponent<T> {\n  //column = input.required<Column<T, unknown>>()\n  //header = input.required<Header<T, unknown>>()\n  table = input.required<Table<T>>()\n}\n```\n\n#### Rendering a TemplateRef\n\nIn order to render a TemplateRef into a specific column header/cell/footer, you can pass the TemplateRef into the column\ndefinition.\n\nYou can access the TemplateRef data via the `$implicit` property, which is valued based on what is passed in the props\nfield of flexRender.\n\nIn most cases, each TemplateRef will be rendered with the $implicit context valued based on the cell type in this way:\n\n- Header: `HeaderContext<T, ?>`\n- Cell: `CellContext<T, ?>`,\n- Footer: `HeaderContext<T, ?>`\n\n```angular-html\n\n<ng-container\n  *flexRender=\"\n              cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n              props: cell.getContext();\n              let cell\n            \"\n>\n  <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n  {{ cell }}\n  <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n  <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n</ng-container>\n\n<ng-template #myCell let-context>\n  <!-- render something with context -->\n</ng-template>\n```\n\nFull example:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport type {\n  CellContext,\n  ColumnDef,\n  HeaderContext,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport {Component, TemplateRef, viewChild} from '@angular/core'\n\n@Component({\n  template: `\n    <tbody>\n      @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n        <tr>\n          @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n            <td>\n              <ng-container\n                *flexRender=\"\n                  cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n                  props: cell.getContext(); // Data given to the TemplateRef\n                  let cell\n                \"\n              >\n                <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n                {{ cell }}\n                <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n                <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n              </ng-container>\n            </td>\n          }\n        </tr>\n      }\n    </tbody>\n\n    <ng-template #customHeader let-context>\n      {{ context.getValue() }}\n    </ng-template>\n    <ng-template #customCell let-context>\n      {{ context.getValue() }}\n    </ng-template>\n  `,\n})\nclass AppComponent {\n  customHeader =\n    viewChild.required<TemplateRef<{ $implicit: HeaderContext<any, any> }>>(\n      'customHeader'\n    )\n  customCell =\n    viewChild.required<TemplateRef<{ $implicit: CellContext<any, any> }>>(\n      'customCell'\n    )\n\n  columns: ColumnDef<unknown>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'customCell',\n      header: () => this.customHeader(),\n      cell: () => this.customCell(),\n    },\n  ]\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Angular Table\n---\n\nThe `@tanstack/angular-table` adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing\nstate the \"angular signals\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates.\n\n## Exports\n\n`@tanstack/angular-table` re-exports all of `@tanstack/table-core`'s APIs and the following:\n\n### `createAngularTable`\n\nAccepts an options function or a computed value that returns the table options, and returns a table.\n\n```ts\nimport {createAngularTable} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nexport class AppComponent {\n  data = signal<Person[]>([])\n\n  table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n    data: this.data(),\n    columns: defaultColumns,\n    getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  }))\n}\n\n// ...render your table in template\n\n```\n\n### `FlexRender`\n\nAn Angular structural directive for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values.\n\nFlexRender supports any type of content supported by Angular:\n\n- A string, or a html string via `innerHTML`\n- A [TemplateRef](https://angular.dev/api/core/TemplateRef)\n- A [Component](https://angular.dev/api/core/Component) wrapped into `FlexRenderComponent`\n\nYou can just use the `cell.renderValue` or `cell.getValue` APIs to render the cells of your table. However,\nthese APIs will only spit out the raw cell values (from accessor functions).\nIf you are using the `cell: () => any` column definition options, you will want to use the `FlexRenderDirective` from the adapter.\n\nCell column definition is **reactive** and runs into an **injection context**, then you can inject services or make use of signals to automatically modify the rendered content.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\n@Component({\n  imports: [FlexRenderDirective],\n  //...\n})\nclass YourComponent {}\n```\n\n```angular-html\n\n<tbody>\n@for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n  <tr>\n    @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container\n          *flexRender=\"\n              cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n              props: cell.getContext();\n              let cell\n            \"\n        >\n          <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n          {{ cell }}\n          <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n          <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n    }\n  </tr>\n}\n</tbody>\n```\n\n#### Rendering a Component\n\nTo render a Component into a specific column header/cell/footer, you can pass a `FlexRenderComponent` instantiated with\nyour `ComponentType, with the ability to include parameters such as inputs, outputs and a custom injector.\n\n```ts\nimport {flexRenderComponent} from \"./flex-render-component\";\nimport {ChangeDetectionStrategy, input, output} from \"@angular/core\";\n\n@Component({\n  template: `\n    ...\n  `,\n  standalone: true,\n  changeDetectionStrategy: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n  host: {\n    '(click)': 'clickEvent.emit($event)'\n  }\n})\nclass CustomCell {\n  readonly content = input.required<string>();\n  readonly cellType = input<MyType>();\n\n  // An output that will emit for every cell click\n  readonly clickEvent = output<Event>();\n}\n\nclass AppComponent {\n  columns: ColumnDef<unknown>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'custom-cell',\n      header: () => {\n        const translateService = inject(TranslateService);\n        return translateService.translate('...');\n      },\n      cell: (context) => {\n        return flexRenderComponent(\n          MyCustomComponent,\n          {\n            injector, // Optional injector\n            inputs: {\n              // Mandatory input since we are using `input.required()\n              content: context.row.original.rowProperty,\n              // cellType? - Optional input\n            },\n            outputs: {\n              clickEvent: () => {\n                // Do something\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        )\n      },\n    },\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nUnderneath, this utilizes\nthe [ViewContainerRef#createComponent](https://angular.dev/api/core/ViewContainerRef#createComponent) api.\nTherefore, you should declare your custom inputs using the @Input decorator or input/model signals.\n\nYou can still access the table cell context through the `injectFlexRenderContext` function, which returns the context\nvalue based on the props you pass to the `FlexRenderDirective`.\n\n```ts\n\n@Component({\n  // ...\n})\nclass CustomCellComponent {\n  // context of a cell component\n  readonly context = injectFlexRenderContext<CellContext<TData, TValue>>();\n  // context of a header/footer component\n  readonly context = injectFlexRenderContext<HeaderContext<TData, TValue>>();\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, you can render a component into a specific column header, cell, or footer by passing the component type\nto the corresponding column definitions. These column definitions will be provided to the `flexRender` directive along\nwith the `context`.\n\n```ts\nclass AppComponent {\n  columns: ColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'select',\n      header: () => TableHeadSelectionComponent<Person>,\n      cell: () => TableRowSelectionComponent<Person>,\n    },\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n```angular-html\n<ng-container\n  *flexRender=\"\n    header.column.columnDef.header;\n    props: header.getContext();\n    let headerCell\n  \"\n>\n  {{ headerCell }}\n</ng-container>\n```\n\nProperties of `context` provided in the `flexRender` directive will be accessible to your component.\nYou can explicitly define the context properties required by your component.\nIn this example, the context provided to flexRender is of type HeaderContext.\nInput signal `table`, which is a property of HeaderContext together with `column` and `header` properties,\nis then defined to be used in the component. If any of the context properties are\nneeded in your component, feel free to use them. Please take note that only input signal is supported,\nwhen defining access to context properties, using this approach.\n\n```angular-ts\n@Component({\n  template: `\n    <input\n      type=\"checkbox\"\n      [checked]=\"table().getIsAllRowsSelected()\"\n      [indeterminate]=\"table().getIsSomeRowsSelected()\"\n      (change)=\"table().toggleAllRowsSelected()\"\n    />\n  `,\n  // ...\n})\nexport class TableHeadSelectionComponent<T> {\n  //column = input.required<Column<T, unknown>>()\n  //header = input.required<Header<T, unknown>>()\n  table = input.required<Table<T>>()\n}\n```\n\n#### Rendering a TemplateRef\n\nIn order to render a TemplateRef into a specific column header/cell/footer, you can pass the TemplateRef into the column\ndefinition.\n\nYou can access the TemplateRef data via the `$implicit` property, which is valued based on what is passed in the props\nfield of flexRender.\n\nIn most cases, each TemplateRef will be rendered with the $implicit context valued based on the cell type in this way:\n\n- Header: `HeaderContext<T, ?>`\n- Cell: `CellContext<T, ?>`,\n- Footer: `HeaderContext<T, ?>`\n\n```angular-html\n\n<ng-container\n  *flexRender=\"\n              cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n              props: cell.getContext();\n              let cell\n            \"\n>\n  <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n  {{ cell }}\n  <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n  <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n</ng-container>\n\n<ng-template #myCell let-context>\n  <!-- render something with context -->\n</ng-template>\n```\n\nFull example:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport type {\n  CellContext,\n  ColumnDef,\n  HeaderContext,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport {Component, TemplateRef, viewChild} from '@angular/core'\n\n@Component({\n  template: `\n    <tbody>\n      @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n        <tr>\n          @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n            <td>\n              <ng-container\n                *flexRender=\"\n                  cell.column.columnDef.cell;\n                  props: cell.getContext(); // Data given to the TemplateRef\n                  let cell\n                \"\n              >\n                <!-- if you want to render a simple string -->\n                {{ cell }}\n                <!-- if you want to render an html string -->\n                <div [innerHTML]=\"cell\"></div>\n              </ng-container>\n            </td>\n          }\n        </tr>\n      }\n    </tbody>\n\n    <ng-template #customHeader let-context>\n      {{ context.getValue() }}\n    </ng-template>\n    <ng-template #customCell let-context>\n      {{ context.getValue() }}\n    </ng-template>\n  `,\n})\nclass AppComponent {\n  customHeader =\n    viewChild.required<TemplateRef<{ $implicit: HeaderContext<any, any> }>>(\n      'customHeader'\n    )\n  customCell =\n    viewChild.required<TemplateRef<{ $implicit: CellContext<any, any> }>>(\n      'customCell'\n    )\n\n  columns: ColumnDef<unknown>[] = [\n    {\n      id: 'customCell',\n      header: () => this.customHeader(),\n      cell: () => this.customCell(),\n    },\n  ]\n}\n```\n"}
